<alert>(b)</alert>
From the values in this table, it appears that the limit is 0.693147.




<alert>(c)</alert>
When we graph the function <m>f(x)</m> we see the graph:




<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/Library__Michigan__Chap1Sec8__Q13_pg-image-1.png" width="41%"/>




This confirms our estimate of the limit.  A reasonable range for <m>x</m>
so that the graph of <m>f(x)</m> enters and leaves a window of height 0.02
around <m>y = 0.693147</m> is <m>-0.0416350861169606 \le x \le 0.0416350861169606</m> and
<m>0.683147\le y\le 0.703147</m>.



